From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: convert applied theme font points to character pixels

Theme font parsing returns positive point sizes, while SPI_SETNONCLIENTMETRICS
and SPI_SETICONTITLELOGFONT expect LOGFONT pixel heights. parse_apply_nonclient
runs under DPI_AWARENESS_CONTEXT_UNAWARE, so convert to negative character
heights at nominal 96 DPI before applying all five nonclient fonts and the
icon-title font. SystemParametersInfo then performs its normal DPI scaling.
This brings actual applied system fonts into agreement with theme font lookup,
instead of persisting positive 10/8 as pixel heights for 10/8 point fonts.
The self-authored theme-metrics regression exercises two actual classic/Luna
application roundtrips and six public SPI/GetThemeSysFont values at 96/144/192.
Mapped sizes can differ by one pixel from direct point conversion at high DPI
because SPI scales the rounded nominal 96 DPI value. No MS binaries change.

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
index ed81369..ad09829 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -796,6 +796,10 @@ static BOOL parse_handle_nonclient_font (struct PARSENONCLIENTSTATE* state,
     if (SUCCEEDED (MSSTYLES_GetFont (lpValue, lpValue + dwValueLen, &lpValue,
         &font)))
     {
+        /* MSSTYLES_GetFont returns points; parse_apply_nonclient applies these
+         * fonts in a DPI-unaware (96 DPI) context. Use character pixel height,
+         * as MSSTYLES_GetPropertyFont does for explicitly requested fonts. */
+        font.lfHeight = -MulDiv(font.lfHeight, 96, 72);
         switch (iPropertyId)
         {
 	  case TMT_CAPTIONFONT:
